course: dictionary
lesson: 12521
title: Desiccation: drying out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Desiccation is a long word for drying something out completely. It is a noun, so it names a process or a state. When you meet it, look at the words around it for clues.
explain: «The desiccation of the riverbed left deep, cracked mud.» The river had dried up and the mud had split, so desiccation must mean the drying out. Check by swapping in your meaning: "The drying out of the riverbed left deep, cracked mud" still makes sense.
explain: Desiccation can also mean the state of being very dry. «Cacti survive desiccation by storing water in their thick stems.» A cactus lives in a dry desert, and storing water is its trick against dryness, so desiccation means the dryness it must survive.
fact: Desiccation means drying something out completely, or removing the water from it.
fact: Food is dried to stop it going off, and this keeps it for longer.
fact: «Desiccation cracks» are the split patterns left in mud or soil when the water dries away.
fact: Long periods of desiccation of land can lead to drought.
fact: A desiccator is a sealed jar that keeps things dry in a lab.
exercise: «Desert animals have tricks to survive desiccation.» What does desiccation mean here? | Growing very tall | *Being very dry, or drying out | Being very wet and cold | Making a loud noise
exercise: «The riverbed was covered in desiccation cracks.» What do the cracks show? | *Mud that has dried out and split | A river flooding its banks | Snow falling on the ground | Sand being blown by the wind
exercise: A scientist keeps dry crystals in a sealed glass jar. Which word names that jar? | *Desiccator | Desk | Dessert | Decanter
test: Why is food dried in science? | To make it wetter | To make it louder | *To keep it for longer | To change its colour only
test: «Protect the seeds from desiccation.» What should you do to the seeds? | Put them in water | *Keep them from drying out | Bury them deep in the soil | Leave them in the hot sun
exam: «The scientists stored the seeds in a desiccator to protect them from desiccation.» What does desiccation mean? | Being covered in snow | *Drying out completely, or the state of being very dry | Growing into a big plant | Making a loud noise
